{"name":"Valkyrie","hex":"#eecc22","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Valkyrie","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of valkyrie."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Valkyrie"}],"entries":[{"title":"Valkyrie","blocks":[{"text":"In Norse mythology, a valkyrie is one of a host of female figures who guide souls of the dead to the god Odin's hall Valhalla. There, the deceased warriors become einherjar. When the einherjar are not preparing for the cataclysmic events of Ragnarök, the valkyries bear them mead. Valkyries also appear as lovers of heroes and other mortals, where they are sometimes described as the daughters of royalty, sometimes accompanied by ravens and sometimes connected to swans, boars or wolves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Historiska_museet_043.jpg/330px-Historiska_museet_043.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valkyrie"},{"title":"Valkyrie (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Valkyrie is a 2008 historical thriller film directed by Bryan Singer, written by Christopher McQuarrie and Nathan Alexander, starring Tom Cruise. The film is set in Nazi Germany during World War II and depicts the 20 July plot in 1944 by German army officers to assassinate Adolf Hitler and to use the Operation Valkyrie national emergency plan to take control of the country. The film was released by American studio United Artists and stars Cruise as Colonel Claus von Stauffenberg, one of the key plotters. The supporting cast includes Kenneth Branagh, Bill Nighy, Eddie Izzard, Terence Stamp, and Tom Wilkinson."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b8/Valkyrie_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valkyrie_(film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Valkyrie_fra_H%C3%A5rby.png/330px-Valkyrie_fra_H%C3%A5rby.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Valkyrie_fra_H%C3%A5rby.png/330px-Valkyrie_fra_H%C3%A5rby.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The \"valkyrie from Hårby\", silver-gilt figurine depicting a female figure with a sword and shield, often interpreted to be a valkyrie.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AValkyrie_fra_H%C3%A5rby.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Hild%2C_Thrud_and_Hl%C3%B8kk_by_Fr%C3%B8lich.jpg/500px-Hild%2C_Thrud_and_Hl%C3%B8kk_by_Fr%C3%B8lich.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Hild%2C_Thrud_and_Hl%C3%B8kk_by_Fr%C3%B8lich.jpg/500px-Hild%2C_Thrud_and_Hl%C3%B8kk_by_Fr%C3%B8lich.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The valkyries Hildr, Þrúðr and Hlökk bearing ale in Valhalla (1895) by Lorenz Frølich","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHild%2C_Thrud_and_Hl%C3%B8kk_by_Fr%C3%B8lich.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/The_Valkyr%C3%A6%2C_by_Johann_Georg_Heck.jpg/500px-The_Valkyr%C3%A6%2C_by_Johann_Georg_Heck.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/The_Valkyr%C3%A6%2C_by_Johann_Georg_Heck.jpg/500px-The_Valkyr%C3%A6%2C_by_Johann_Georg_Heck.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Valkyræ, by Johann Georg Heck","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Valkyr%C3%A6%2C_by_Johann_Georg_Heck.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Walkyrien_by_Emil_Doepler.jpg/500px-Walkyrien_by_Emil_Doepler.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_con